<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick VI of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1768–1839</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick VI was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from 1808 and regent from 1784, also ruling the duchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> and Holstein. As regent he backed the abolition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> in 1788. His alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> after the British bombardment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> in 1807 ended in the loss of Norway to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in 1814. He then ruled Denmark as an absolute monarch.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-vi-of-denmark.jpg" alt="Frederick VI of Denmark" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Carl Gröger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fiedrichvidenmark.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
